#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0119 expect=noViolation domain=CO
#note "A three-member contiguous series with correct widths: the run [0..2] is contiguous, and the min_length test EXEMPTS the terminal member, so COVAL2's width of 60 is conformant while COVAL and COVAL1 both reach 200. NOT vacuous: narrowing COVAL1 to 199 makes this same file fire, which is the -invalid_short_non_terminal sibling. M3-D22 moved this rule's Executability from 'Fully Executable' to 'Partially Executable - Possible Underreporting' with no Check change: column_series_metadata reads only DECLARED column lengths and never a data cell, so the sheet's Condition ('Comment value > 200 characters in length') cannot be detected on an unsplit comment. Reading the data would need a length-of-value operator the engine does not have."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset CO label="Comments"
col STUDYID type=Char length=12 label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char length=2  label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char length=20 label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col COVAL   type=Char length=200 label="Comment"
col COVAL1  type=Char length=200 label="Comment Part 1"
col COVAL2  type=Char length=60  label="Comment Part 2"
---
S1 | CO | 001 | 1 | chunk one | chunk two | chunk three
S1 | CO | 002 | 1 | only chunk |  |
---
